     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Ah, the million-dollar question! The meaning of life is a question that has plagued philosophers, theologians, scientists, and individuals for centuries. There's no single, universally accepted answer, and that's kind of the beauty of it. It's a deeply personal and evolving exploration.\n",
      "\n",
      "Here's a breakdown of common perspectives and things to consider:\n",
      "\n",
      "**1. The Nihilistic View:**\n",
      "\n",
      "*   **Core Idea:** Life has no inherent meaning. We are born, we live, and we die, and there's no cosmic purpose behind it.\n",
      "*   **Implications:** This might sound depressing, but it can also be liberating. If there's no inherent meaning, you're free to create your own.\n",
      "\n",
      "**2. The Absurdist View:**\n",
      "\n",
      "*   **Core Idea:**  We have an innate desire to find meaning in a meaningless universe. This creates a fundamental conflict, which is the \"absurd.\"\n",
      "*   **Implications:**  Embrace the absurdity. Live passionately and rebelliously, even in the face of meaninglessness.  Think Albert Camus' \"The Myth of Sisyphus.\"\n",
      "\n",
      "**3. The Religious/Spiritual View:**\n",
      "\n",
      "*   **Core Idea:**  Life has a meaning ordained by a higher power or connected to a larger spiritual reality. This meaning might involve serving God, fulfilling a divine plan, achieving enlightenment, or joining with the universe.\n",
      "*   **Implications:**  Follow the teachings of your religion or spiritual tradition. Find purpose in devotion, prayer, service, and striving for spiritual growth.\n",
      "\n",
      "**4. The Meaning-Through-Purpose View:**\n",
      "\n",
      "*   **Core Idea:**  Meaning is found in pursuing a purpose or set of goals. This purpose can be anything that gives your life direction and significance.\n",
      "*   **Implications:**  Identify your values, passions, and talents. Set goals that align with these things.  Dedicate yourself to something bigger than yourself. This could be your career, family, a cause, or a creative pursuit.\n",
      "\n",
      "**5. The Meaning-Through-Relationships View:**\n",
      "\n",
      "*   **Core Idea:**  Meaning is found in connecting with others, building meaningful relationships, and contributing to the well-being of others.\n",
      "*   **Implications:**  Invest in your relationships with family, friends, and community. Practice empathy, compassion, and kindness.  Seek to understand and support those around you.\n",
      "\n",
      "**6. The Meaning-Through-Experience View:**\n",
      "\n",
      "*   **Core Idea:**  Meaning is found in experiencing life to the fullest, embracing new adventures, and appreciating the beauty and wonder of the world.\n",
      "*   **Implications:**  Step outside your comfort zone.  Travel, learn new things, try new hobbies, and cultivate a sense of awe and wonder.  Practice mindfulness and appreciate the present moment.\n",
      "\n",
      "**7. The Meaning-Through-Growth View:**\n",
      "\n",
      "*   **Core Idea:** Meaning is found in constantly learning, growing, and striving to become the best version of yourself.\n",
      "*   **Implications:** Embrace challenges, learn from your mistakes, and never stop seeking self-improvement.  Focus on developing your strengths, overcoming your weaknesses, and expanding your horizons.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Ultimately, the meaning of life is what you make it.**\n",
      "\n",
      "Here are some questions to help you find your own meaning:\n",
      "\n",
      "*   **What are you passionate about?**\n",
      "*   **What do you value most?**\n",
      "*   **What impact do you want to have on the world?**\n",
      "*   **What brings you joy and fulfillment?**\n",
      "*   **What are you good at?**\n",
      "*   **What problems do you want to solve?**\n",
      "\n",
      "Think about these questions, experiment with different activities and perspectives, and see what resonates with you. The answer may change over time, and that's okay. The journey of searching for meaning is just as important as the destination.\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import google.generativeai as genai\n",
    "\n",
    "genai.configure(api_key=\"your_api_key_here\")\n",
    "model = genai.GenerativeModel(\"gemini-2.0-flash\")\n",
    "response = model.generate_content(\"what is the meaning of life?\")\n",
    "print(response.text)"
   ]
  },
